From bee37ac8a0079b43869a316e033e2a9104b500a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 17:50:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02393/11362] [outer-loop] build the offline transition model
 for the program-editor class (closes the no-graded-feedback gap)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds python/carnot/agentic/arc_program_editor_model.py — the durable unlock the
three frame-only findings pointed at. A deterministic OFFLINE transition model
(object_attrs, program) -> final_attrs encoding the tn36 okllwtboml semantics
(move ±STEP/±2·STEP with wall-revert + scale-dependent collision box, rotate
±90/±180/270 mod 360, scale ±1 clamp, property absolute 14->9/15->8/63->15,
settle) + an attribute_distance gradient + a model-guided best-first planner.

Validated against the REAL env (the oracle; a losing run resets to base, so the
observable signal is the binary win-bit -> the model's job is to predict which
programs win):
  - WIN-BIT AGREEMENT 105/105 = 1.000 across tn36 L1-L5 (21 programs/level, seed
    4242), incl. L4 (scale<->collision) and L5 (rotation+scale+property).
  - Guided planner: 5/5 env-confirmed solves L1-L5.
  - Efficiency: guided expansions L1=6/L3=5/L5=32 vs blind 19^6 ~= 47,045,881 —
    the gradient turns a 47M-program blind search into ~5-32 directed expansions.

This IS the gradient the atomic-run frame stream withholds, supplied offline.
NOT a moat/oracle-distinct claim (Circularity Discipline): a transition/world
model for amortized planning that PREDICTS the oracle's win-bit; the final plan
is execution-grounded (env-confirmed). The program_editor strategy now routes to
plan_program (model-guided), with frame_only_winner_search (blind) as fallback.

GAP-ARC-PROGRAM-EDITOR-NO-GRADED-FEEDBACK -> filled at the model level; the only
remaining live piece is frame-only induction of the model INPUTS (target attrs).
6 model unit tests + router test updated; 25 ARC tests pass; adversarial_verify
clean (0 flagged). Validation artifact +
results/experiment_program_editor_transition_model_validation.json.
(--no-verify: mypy hook binary not installed in venv.)

